3. Build platform and framework components
------------------------------------------

The firmware is built for the Espressif ESP32 platform using the Arduino-ESP32
core.

Build platform:

- Arduino-ESP32 core
  Version used by this project: 3.3.12
  Source:
  https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32

- ESP-IDF components bundled with or used by Arduino-ESP32
  Version and component licenses depend on the Arduino-ESP32 distribution.
  Source:
  https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf
  Primary component license: LGPL-2.1 (and others; see Espressif / Arduino
  ESP32 licensing for the exact component list).

Arduino-ESP32 and ESP-IDF contain multiple components with different
copyright and license terms. Their licenses must be reviewed from the exact
versions used to build a particular firmware release.

The following framework components are used by the boot managers where
applicable:

- WiFi, WebServer, HTTPClient
- LittleFS, FS
- Preferences, NVS APIs
- OTA and partition APIs
- FreeRTOS
- QR code generation (beta)

These components are not relicensed under the MIT License of this repository.
The applicable notices from Arduino-ESP32 and ESP-IDF remain in effect.

Binary releases that link LGPL libraries must allow relinking or replacement
of those libraries as required by their licenses.

3.1 Prebuilt bootloader (ESP-IDF, Apache-2.0)
---------------------------------------------

This repository ships prebuilt second-stage bootloaders built from ESP-IDF and
modified by this repository:

- ats-mini-recovery-beta/bootloader.bin
- ats-mini-recovery-lite/bootloader.bin

and a patch describing the modification:

- ats-mini-recovery-beta/bootloader.patch

ESP-IDF is distributed by Espressif under the Apache License 2.0 (some
components under other licenses). The bootloader files above are derivative
works of ESP-IDF. Their build and modification are documented in
ats-mini-recovery-beta/bootloader.md and ats-mini-recovery-beta/bootloader.patch.

When redistributing these files, retain the applicable copyright and
attribution notices and include a copy of the Apache License 2.0
(LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). The bootloader is provided "AS IS", without
warranties or conditions of any kind, as stated in that license.

